 which or whom the oath is taken; {#satyaM SapAmi te pAdapaNkajasparSena#}
 <ls>K.</ls>; <ls>Ghaṭ. 22</ls>; {#aSapta nihnuvAnA'sO sItAyE smaramohitaH#} <ls>Bk. 8. 74</ls>;
 {#prema jijYAsamAnAByastAByo'Sapsata kAminaH#} <ls n="Bk.">8. 33</ls>; sometimes {#Sap#}
 governs a cognate accusative; {#sahasraSo'sO SapaTAnaSapyat#} <ls>Bk. 3. 32</ls>; <ls>Ms. 8. 110</ls>.
.²3 To blame, scold, revile, abuse (with <ab>dat.</ab> or by itself); {#dvizadBapaScA-SapaMstaTA#}

 <ls>Bk. 17. 4</ls>; {#prativAcamadatta keSavaH SapamAnAya na cediBUBuje#} <ls>Śi. 16. 25</ls>.
